    (sess, 10, 'Do you give staff paid volunteering days each year?', 'A11', 'No confident match in the knowledge base: the closest entries are listed under Sources, but they may not answer this question. It needs an answer written by a person.', 0, 0.3046325086857213, '[{"id":"KB-0020","score":0.3046325086857213},{"id":"KB-0015","score":0.297750377841337}]'::jsonb, 0.3046325086857213, 'no', NULL, NULL, 'en', 'voyage-4', 'claude-haiku-5-5', 'KB-0020', 'The entries cover security awareness training and GDPR compliance; neither mentions paid volunteering days or any employee leave or volunteering policy, so the question cannot be answered from them.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-22.3 (calibrate split)', 'insufficient_evidence', ARRAY[]::text[], NULL, '2026-10-25T07:22:44.961Z'::timestamptz),
    (sess, 11, 'How do you manage the risks of open-source components in your software?', 'A12', 'We manage open-source software risk through a policy that requires legal review of licenses and security review of components before adoption. Software composition analysis (SCA) tooling continuously monitors production and development dependencies for known CVEs, and developers receive automated alerts when newly disclosed vulnerabilities affect components they use. We also maintain a curated internal catalog of approved open-source libraries so that teams can adopt vetted components.

